{"id":"write-english-cenc-tibet-m71","capability":"write_english","what":"中国地震台网中心正式测定西藏南部 Mw 7.1，中文稿与原文都点名 CENC 与 USGS","match":{"includes":["中国地震台网中心正式测定","Mw 7.1"]},"reply":{"title":"Magnitude 7.1 earthquake strikes southern Tibet near the Yarlung Tsangpo suture","summary":"The China Earthquake Networks Center recorded a magnitude 7.1 earthquake in southern Tibet at 06:12 Beijing time on 21 November 2026, at a depth of 12 km. The USGS put the same event at Mw 7.0 and placed the epicenter on the Yarlung Tsangpo suture zone, about 38 km from the nearest county seat. Both agencies report ongoing aftershocks but no confirmed casualties.","reason":"A first-hour measurement from the national network, with the two agencies' magnitudes stated side by side instead of averaged."},"author":"英文编辑（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文稿与原文）"}
{"id":"write-english-noaa-hurricane","capability":"write_english","what":"NHC 对一场飓风的路径与强度通报","match":{"includes":["Hurricane Warning","Lesser Antilles"]},"reply":{"title":"Hurricane turns north, keeping the Lesser Antilles under warning","summary":"The National Hurricane Center reported that the hurricane was moving north at 14 km/h on 22 November 2026, with maximum sustained winds of 130 km/h. A hurricane warning remains in effect for the Lesser Antilles, while the storm's core is forecast to stay east of the islands. The center expects gradual weakening after 48 hours.","reason":"The forecast track and the warning area together answer the reader's first question: does this storm reach land, and when."},"author":"英文编辑（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文稿与原文）"}